# The kitty keyboard protocol's key code is the unshifted key, which the host
# reports. Ctrl+Shift+1 on the US layout makes the keysym exclam, and its
# unshifted key is 1, so under flag 1 it is sent with the code 49. Where the
# host reports no unshifted key, because AltGr chose the symbol, as AltGr+Q
# makes @ on a German layout, vtium sends the symbol the key made.
# spec: kitty's Comprehensive keyboard handling in terminals: Key codes, Disambiguate escape codes; ADR-1005 D2, D9 and D13 slice 3
# capability: key-kitty-unshifted-key
size 20 2
needs key-forms
send "\e[>1u"
cmd key;sym=21;ascii=21;unicode=21;unshifted=31;mods=5
cmd key;sym=40;ascii=40;unicode=40;mods=8
check
reply "\e[49;6u\e[64;3u"
